---
import RootLayout from "~/layouts/RootLayout.astro";

const metadata = {
  title: "A Music App That Pays South African Artists Fairly — DeeMusiq",
  description:
    "DeeMusiq's built-in token wallet lets fans stream and top up, and artists keep ownership of their music and withdraw earnings through South African payment rails.",
  keywords:
    "music app that pays artists, South African artist payouts, fair music streaming, artist wallet, stream and earn, DeeMusiq payouts",
};
---

<RootLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="p-4 md:p-16 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="h1">A Music App That Pays South African Artists Fairly</h1>
    <br />
    <p class="text-surface-500">
      Artists keep ownership of their music — and get paid when it moves.
      DeeMusiq bakes fair payouts into the app itself with a built-in token
      wallet and South African payment rails.
    </p>
    <br /><br />

    <h2 class="h2">How it works</h2>
    <br />
    <h3 class="h3">1. Artists set their presence</h3>
    <br />
    <p>
      An artist claims their profile on DeeMusiq and puts their music in front
      of fans on their own terms. Ownership of the music stays with the artist
      — DeeMusiq is the stage, not the landlord.
    </p>
    <br />
    <h3 class="h3">2. Fans stream and top up</h3>
    <br />
    <p>
      Listeners stream the catalog and can top up the artist's token wallet
      directly inside the app — whether they're vibing to
      <a href="/stream-amapiano-gqom-afrobeats" class="underline">amapiano, gqom or afrobeats</a>
      or a brand-new drop. Support flows from fan to artist without a label
      skimming the middle.
    </p>
    <br />
    <h3 class="h3">3. Artists withdraw via ZA rails</h3>
    <br />
    <p>
      Earnings land in the artist's wallet and can be withdrawn through
      familiar South African payment rails — rand in, rand out, no waiting on
      international royalty pipelines.
    </p>
    <br />

    <h2 class="h2">Fairness built in, not bolted on</h2>
    <br />
    <p>
      DeeMusiq is a
      <a href="/spotube-alternative" class="underline">Spotube alternative</a>
      with a mission: the open-source player everyone loved, extended with a
      native African catalog, offline DRM-protected listening, and a wallet
      that makes streaming sustainable for local artists. We also take your
      data as seriously as your money — see our
      <a href="/privacy" class="underline">privacy and POPIA stance</a>.
    </p>
    <br /><br />

    <a href="/downloads" class="btn preset-filled-primary-300-700">
      Download DeeMusiq
    </a>
  </section>
</RootLayout>
